mode: "100644"
text: "# Audit template, math + two worked examples\n\n## The capture template (one row per competitor)\n| Field | What to note (public only) |\n|---|---|\n| Type | direct / aspirational / adjacent |\n| Positioning | the one-line promise they make |\n| Pillars | 3–5 recurring themes |\n| Formats & mix | Reels / carousels / text / video / Stories — rough % |\n| Cadence | posts/week per platform |\n| Hooks & tone | how they open; voice |\n| Top posts (public) | 3–5 high-engagement posts + the likely *why* |\n| Engagement rate | est. ER (engagements ÷ followers ÷ posts) — flag as estimate |\n| Growth trend | rising / flat / falling (directional) |\n| Paid | any ad-library creative running |\n| AI/LLM visibility | cited by ChatGPT/Gemini/Claude for category queries? |\n\n## The math (keep it honest)\n- **Engagement rate (public est.):** `engagements ÷ followers ÷ posts` over a window. It's an\n  **estimate** (you can't see reach/saves on others) — state that.\n- **Share of voice:** `your mentions ÷ total mentions across the set` for a topic/keyword.\n- **Relative read:** compare each rival to the **set median**, and your trend vs theirs — not to the\n  platform average.\n\n## The white-space matrix\nPlot **content pillars (rows) × formats or funnel stages (columns)**; mark where each competitor is\nstrong. **Empty/weak cells the audience wants = your white space.** Also scan for: an unclaimed POV, a\nneglected platform, a service/voice gap, an underserved sub-audience.\n\n## Worked example 1 — find the gap (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\nFIELD: 6 bookkeeping/finance-tool accounts (3 direct, 2 aspirational, 1 adjacent creator)\nWORKS: the set wins on carousels of \"tips\"; one aspirational account dominates LinkedIn SOV.\nWHITE SPACE: nobody does short, dry founder-POV video on the *emotional* side of tax (all how-to, no relief).\nTRANSLATE: claim \"calm finance\" POV; pillar = \"the panic, fixed\"; format = 15s Reels (route ai-video).\nTEST: 4 Reels over 4 weeks; KPI = saves + profile visits vs our carousel baseline. -> social-strategy\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 — relative benchmark, not vanity (warm studio voice)\n```\nQUESTION: \"Competitor has 500k followers, we have 12k -- are we losing?\"\nREAD: their est. ER ~0.3% (large but low engagement); ours ~4% on saves. Relative, we over-index.\nSOV: we hold ~22% of category conversation on \"first-time freelancer tax\" -- a niche they ignore.\nWHITE SPACE: that exact beginner sub-audience; their content skews advanced.\nTRANSLATE: double down on beginner pillar in our voice; don't chase their follower count. -> social-strategy\n```\n\nBoth: read brand-profile + audience-research first; public signals only; engagement-weighted +\nrelative; estimates flagged; gap translated into the brand's own voice and tested with KPIs. Feeds\n`social-strategy`, `content-pillars`, and `content-recycling` (which proven angles to double down on).\n"
